    },
    "excluded_steps": [],
    "format_errors": [],
    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 137,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 138,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 27,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 28,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: First, we need to rewrite both equations in standard form to identify the type of conic sections they represent and their centers."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 440,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 442,
        "char_start": 140,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 197,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 198,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: For the first equation \\(x^2 + y^2 + 6x - 24y + 72 = 0\\), complete the square for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n\\[x^2 + 6x + y^2 - 24y + 72 = 0\\]\n\\[(x+3)^2 - 9 + (y-12)^2 - 144 + 72 = 0\\]\n\\[(x+3)^2 + (y-12)^2 - 81 = 0\\]\n\\[(x+3)^2 + (y-12)^2 = 81\\]\nThis is a circle with center \\((-3, 12)\\) and radius \\(9\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 756,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 758,
        "char_start": 444,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 379,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 380,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: For the second equation \\(x^2 - y^2 + 6x + 16y - 46 = 0\\), complete the square for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\):\n\\[x^2 + 6x - y^2 + 16y - 46 = 0\\]\n\\[(x+3)^2 - 9 - (y-8)^2 + 64 - 46 = 0\\]\n\\[(x+3)^2 - (y-8)^2 - 9 + 18 = 0\\]\n\\[(x+3)^2 - (y-8)^2 = -9\\]\n\\[(y-8)^2 - (x+3)^2 = 9\\]\nThis is a hyperbola centered at \\((-3, 8)\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 945,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 946,
        "char_start": 760,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 432,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 433,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: The center of the circle is \\((-3, 12)\\) and the center of the hyperbola is \\((-3, 8)\\). Both have the same x-coordinate, which means the line connecting the centers is vertical."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1039,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1041,
        "char_start": 948,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 463,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 464,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: The distance between the centers of the circle and the hyperbola is \\(|12 - 8| = 4\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1370,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1372,
        "char_start": 1043,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 546,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 547,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Since the line connecting the centers is vertical, the points of intersection will be symmetric about this line. Therefore, the sum of the distances from any point of intersection to \\((-3, 12)\\) plus the distance from that point to \\((-3, 8)\\) will be twice the distance between the centers, which is \\(2 \\times 4 = 8\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1705,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1706,
        "char_start": 1374,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 630,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 631,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: There are four points of intersection, and the sum of the distances from these points to \\((-3, 2)\\) can be calculated by noting that the sum of the distances from each pair of symmetric points to \\((-3, 2)\\) will be the same as the sum of the distances from the centers to \\((-3, 2)\\) plus the distance between the centers."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1861,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1862,
        "char_start": 1708,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 703,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 704,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Calculate the distance from \\((-3, 12)\\) to \\((-3, 2)\\):\n\\[|12 - 2| = 10\\]\nCalculate the distance from \\((-3, 8)\\) to \\((-3, 2)\\):\n\\[|8 - 2| = 6\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1930,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1931,
        "char_start": 1864,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 734,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 735,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: The total sum of the distances is:\n\\[10 + 6 + 10 + 6 = 32\\]"
      }
    ]
  },
